                            <comment id="14389376" author="githubbot" created="Tue, 31 Mar 2015 20:47:09 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;GitHub user felixcheung opened a pull request:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/19&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/19&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-17&quot; title=&quot;PySpark Interpreter should allow starting with a specific version of Python&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-17&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-17&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; PySpark Interpreter should allow starting with a specific version of Python&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    Add PYSPARK_PYTHON.&lt;br/&gt;
    We could also add PYSPARK_DRIVER_PYTHON (Zeppelin Interpreter is the driver) but it doesn&apos;t seem to be documented, and more importantly running different Python between driver and worker can cause errors.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;http://spark.apache.org/docs/1.3.0/configuration.html&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://spark.apache.org/docs/1.3.0/configuration.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;


